  "observations": "Root ordered second reading: whole and both actual supplied halves were viewed before the image-first receipt and text-open event. All prose, accents, punctuation, symbols, indices, products, arrows, inequalities, underlines, replacements and cancellation states were compared against the consolidated page. All27 fresh audit crops were personally viewed. The isolated faint acute in fermée is retained; inversible is read as typed. The first cancelled pour is broadened to par|pour from its letter spacing and surviving forms. The first Hom base is now uncertain between plain S and a distinct doubled alphabet: the double impression itself is clear. All nine earlier doubtful loci were reexamined; obscured a)/b), the mark before fidèlement, the second cancelled pour, cancelled G, unreadable cancelled word and first 2|1 reference remain unresolved. The preliminary image-first impression that all lower text was ordinary reverse show-through was corrected on closer inspection: the four covered cancelled passages are retained, including the last vertically reflected line. Their physically obscured text remains explicitly doubtful. Top2 is manuscript numbering; bottom33 is archival and remains a comment. No context or mathematical proof check was used.",
